---
import Education from '../../layouts/Education.astro';
import SiteSymbol from '../../components/SiteSymbol.astro';
import type { SymbolName } from '../../lib/site-symbols';
import { clubMeetingSymbols } from '../../lib/list-identities';
import TeachingDownloads from '../../components/TeachingDownloads.astro';
import {beginnerMeetings,clubRoles,clubHandover,clubInvitation,clubConstitution} from '../../data/education-kit.mjs';
import {url} from '../../lib/site';
const roleSymbols: Record<string, SymbolName> = {
  Facilitator: 'dialogue', 'Access coordinator': 'doorway',
  Timekeeper: 'clock', 'Notes and handover': 'notes',
};
const constitutionSymbols: Record<string, SymbolName> = {
  'Purpose and draft status': 'target', 'Locally eligible membership': 'people',
  'Rotating roles': 'loop', 'Meetings and decisions': 'calendar', 'Access and discussion': 'speech',
  'Funds and authority': 'scale', 'Affiliation and recognition': 'badge', 'Handover and privacy': 'lock',
};
---
<Education title="Start with one good question." description="A practical starter for a student-led reading group, campus club or educator-supported extracurricular group." filePath="src/data/education-kit.mjs" active="clubs" sourceIds={['mason-student-organizations','mason-student-contact','mclean-clubs','woodson-clubs']}>
  <a slot="actions" class="btn" href="#first-meetings">Plan the first four meetings</a><a slot="actions" class="btn btn-ghost" href={url('/programs/university-chapters/#pw-four-starter')}>Review the four-meeting starter in the workspace</a>
  <section><h2 id="start-a-club">Find people and the right local route.</h2><ol class="education-step-list"><li><SiteSymbol name="fileSearch" size="inline" /> <strong>Check what already exists.</strong> A discussion within an existing philosophy, civic, service or nonprofit group may be useful. Ask interested students rather than requesting a membership list.</li><li><SiteSymbol name="school" size="inline" /> <strong>Check the campus or school process.</strong> Confirm who may organize, whether a sponsor is needed, recognition steps, room access, branding and any event rules. Do not use an institution’s name or logo as evidence of approval.</li><li><SiteSymbol name="calendar" size="inline" /> <strong>Offer one meeting without a fundraising target.</strong> Bring the fictional case and a clear ending time. Invite different views and make participation possible without an account, device or personal story.</li><li><SiteSymbol name="fork" size="inline" /> <strong>Decide together whether to continue.</strong> Keep the next action, owner role and open question. A useful first meeting does not establish a recognized chapter or a proven teaching benefit.</li></ol><p>At Mason, the public <a href="https://si.gmu.edu/rso/">student organization guidance</a> describes student-led registration, with detailed HUB steps behind sign-in. The school examples below are local examples, not a common approval form. School groups should begin with an adult educator and the <a href={url('/learn/schools/')}>school guide</a>.</p><TeachingDownloads ids={['club-starter','student-worksheet']} /></section>
  <section id="first-meetings"><p class="eyebrow">Beginner sequence · proposed 50-minute meetings</p><h2>Four meetings that leave something useful.</h2>{beginnerMeetings.map(meeting=><article class="education-session"><p class="eyebrow">Meeting {meeting.number}</p><h3><SiteSymbol name={clubMeetingSymbols[meeting.number]} size="inline" /> {meeting.title}</h3><p>{meeting.activity}</p><p><strong>Suggested timing.</strong> {meeting.timing}</p><p><strong>Take away.</strong> {meeting.output}</p></article>)}<p>The <a href={url('/programs/university-chapters/#pw-four-starter')}>chapter workspace</a> can prepare this four-meeting starter for explicit review, with tasks, a draft constitution and exports. The six-session fictional example remains available. Applying either reviewed kit replaces that local workspace only after its existing discard checks; the stored format is unchanged.</p></section>
  <section><h2 id="club-handover">Share the work, then hand it over.</h2><div class="education-grid">{clubRoles.map(role=><article class="education-card"><h3><SiteSymbol name={roleSymbols[role.role]} size="inline" /> {role.role}</h3><p>{role.detail}</p></article>)}</div><h3>A handover card without learner records</h3><ul>{clubHandover.map(item=><li>{item}</li>)}</ul><p>Keep private comments, personal stories, contact lists and account credentials out of shared notes. Learners can keep their own worksheets. Use fictional examples for a public contribution unless the appropriate permissions and editorial checks are in place.</p></section>
  <section><h2 id="club-invitation">An editable invitation</h2><div class="education-callout"><p>{clubInvitation}</p></div><h2 id="club-constitution">A draft constitution to adapt</h2><p>This template does not register a group. Eligible students or adult school staff should adapt it to current local requirements.</p>{clubConstitution.map(clause=><article class="education-session"><h3><SiteSymbol name={constitutionSymbols[clause.title]} size="inline" /> {clause.title}</h3><p>{clause.text}</p></article>)}</section>
</Education>
